ine, we see that $y=1$ is a source.\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. From the phase line, we see that $y=-2$ is a sink.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." 13194139535952 true] [17592186376108 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376109 13194139535952 true] [17592186376108 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376110 13194139535952 true] [17592186376108 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376111 13194139535952 true] [17592186376108 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376112 13194139535952 true] [17592186376108 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376113 13194139535952 true] [17592186376108 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535952 true] [17592186376108 1041 "selection" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376108 1104 #edb/ref 17592186376112 13194139535952 true] [17592186376108 1110 #uuid "87f3885f-d5ff-5d88-a6a1-e132c9f4c7b4" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376109 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376109 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535952 true] [17592186376109 1111 #uuid "5fd8f14d-2fc8-549a-8b79-a766a644a134" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376110 1034 "I only" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376110 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535952 true] [17592186376110 1111 #uuid "1a5124b5-2316-5d80-b0ac-6a54ba65ca89" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376111 1034 "III only" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376111 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535952 true] [17592186376111 1111 #uuid "e7790410-4b02-5f52-98fd-6c0d31b227a3" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376112 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376112 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535952 true] [17592186376112 1111 #uuid "52c0b255-d908-5577-9904-274eb32b9f99" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376113 1034 "II only" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376113 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535952 true] [17592186376113 1111 #uuid "bdf13bc1-9dc5-5045-bfa1-22175245e109" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376114 1017 #edb/ref 17592186376115 13194139535952 true] [17592186376114 1089 "q-340352" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376114 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535952 true] [17592186376114 1100 "Which of the following statements is true regarding the equilibrium solutions of ${y}^{′}={y}^{2}+y-12?$" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376114 1113 #uuid "e59e11c9-19f2-5fd2-8af6-91ba29833c0c" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376114 1145 "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nFirst, we need to find the equilibrium solutions. So, we solve $f(y)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(y) & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}+y-12 & =0 \\\\ (y+4)(y-3) & =0 \\\\ y & =-4,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equilibrium solutions are $y=-4$ and $y=3.$ \n\nNow, we analyze the sign of $f(y)$ using a sign table, as follows:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-4)$ | $(-4,3)$ | $(3,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y+4$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $y-3$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $f(y)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nSo, we have that $f(y)$ is positive for $y\\in (-\\infty ,-4)\\cup (3,\\infty ),$ and negative for $y\\in (-4,3).$\n\nWe can now draw the phase line for this equation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071359/assets/c2bb2cbc11afb9bb2b25fb2105d19c2748541592c77bcecab342db69834b4fe2.png)\n\nFinally, we classify the equilibrium solutions:\n\n- $y=-4$ is a sink because the nearby solutions converge toward this point.\n\n- $y=3$ is a source because the nearby solutions diverge away from this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$y=-4$ is a sink, and $y=3$ is a source\"." 13194139535952 true] [17592186376115 1000 #e