e line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nLet's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Notice that the arrow just above the point $y=4$ points upward, and the arrow just below it points downward. In other words, both arrows point *away* from  $y=4.$ This means that $y=4$ is a source.\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that the arrow just above the point $y=1$ points downward, and the arrow just below it points downward too. In other words, both arrows point in the *same* direction on either side oft $y=1.$This means that $y=1$ is a node.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." 13194139535952 true] [17592186376129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376130 13194139535952 true] [17592186376129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376131 13194139535952 true] [17592186376129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376132 13194139535952 true] [17592186376129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376133 13194139535952 true] [17592186376129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376134 13194139535952 true] [17592186376129 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535952 true] [17592186376129 1041 "selection" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376129 1104 #edb/ref 17592186376132 13194139535952 true] [17592186376129 1110 #uuid "53f18f4c-531e-56b5-9105-65fe30dd7f01" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376130 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376130 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535952 true] [17592186376130 1111 #uuid "10709a2d-63e2-5053-9dcc-f712e0fc9edf" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376131 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376131 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535952 true] [17592186376131 1111 #uuid "f8863a23-1c5f-5ffa-a305-8264321a8e7d" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376132 1034 "I only" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376132 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535952 true] [17592186376132 1111 #uuid "8d590707-5683-54b1-aa50-dced45d3c1ee" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376133 1034 "III only" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376133 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535952 true] [17592186376133 1111 #uuid "93c86398-e49e-5d7a-84f1-359a7233c575" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376134 1034 "II only" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376134 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535952 true] [17592186376134 1111 #uuid "847e8962-ec98-5c24-bf60-26a29774b1bd" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376135 1017 #edb/ref 17592186376136 13194139535952 true] [17592186376135 1089 "q-98762" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376135 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535952 true] [17592186376135 1100 "Which of the following statements is true regarding the equilibrium solutions of ${y}^{′}=2+y-{y}^{2}?$" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376135 1113 #uuid "26ed5480-33c8-5f24-be06-ea5c8236ac1a" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376135 1145 "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nFirst, we need to find the equilibrium solutions. So, we solve $f(y)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(y) & =0 \\\\ 2+y-{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ -({y}^{2}-y-2) & =0 \\\\ -(y+1)(y-2) & =0 \\\\ y & =-1,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equilibrium solutions are $y=-1$ and $y=2.$ \n\nNow, we analyze the sign of $f(y)$ using a sign table, as follows:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-1)$ | $(-1,2)$ | $(2,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-(y+1)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| $y-2$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $f(y)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\nSo, we have that $f(y)$ is negative for $y\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (2,\\infty ),$ and positive for $y\\in (-1,2).$\n\nWe can now draw the phase line for this equation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071359/assets/9230d847daa518edfaad43f6552a48c2b3cac9523a1e9ecad8624851080e00ea.png)\n\nFinally, we classify the equilibrium solutions:\n\n- $y=-1$ is a source because the nearby solutions diverge away from this point.\n\n- $y=2$ is a sink because the nearby solutions converge toward this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$y=-1$ is a source, and $y=2$ is a sink\"." 13194139535952 true] [17592186376136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376137 13194139535952 true] [17592186376136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376138 13194139535952 true] [17592186376136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376139 13194139535952 true] [17592186376136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376140 13194139535952 true] [17592186376136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376141 13194139535952 true] [17592186376136 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535952 true] [17592186376136 1041 "selection" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376136 1104 #edb/ref 17592186376139 13194139535952 true] [17592186376136 1110 #uuid "88fb2801-d362-51d7-9bac-cb9f73be7aa6" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376137 1034 "$y=-1$ is a source, and $y=2$ is a node" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376137 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535952 true] [17592186376137 1111 #uuid "2ac9fc4e-c55c-5f62-b3e5-7f438f2a2922" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376138 1034 "$y=-1$ and $y=2$ are both sinks" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376138 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535952 true] [17592186376138 1111 #uuid "bbee1050-db00-5617-9d18-842b1d40cce3" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376139 1034 "$y=-1$ is a source, and $y=2$ is a sink" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376139 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535952 true] [17592186376139 1111 #uuid "609e3f91-a0a8-5b98-b6bd-b04e9fb74760" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376140 1034 "$y=-1$ and $y=2$ are both sources" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376140 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535952 true] [17592186376140 1111 #uuid "e87ddba3-fdd2-593f-9d17-72b4c80ffd0e" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376141 1034 "$y=-1$ is a sink, and $y=2$ is a source" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376141 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535952 true] [17592186376141 1111 #uuid "3a7ca8a5-0e83-5f5c-8e2a-bf764acf3c01" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376142 1017 #edb/ref 17592186376143 13194139535952 true] [17592186376142 1089 "q-98764" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376142 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535952 true] [17592186376142 1100 "Which of the following statements is true regarding the equilibrium solutions of ${y}^{′}=(y+2)({y}^{2}+2)?$" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376142 1113 #uuid "8d8bc14b-d6cd-5708-b7ce-c5b5f753bf7e" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376142 1145 "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nFirst, we need to find the equilibrium solutions. So, we solve $f(y)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(y) & =0 \\\\ (y+2)({y}^{2}+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equilibrium solution is $y=-2.$ \n\nNow, we analyze the sign of $f(y)$ using a sign table, as follows:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-2)$ | $(2,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y+2$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| ${y}^{2}+2$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $f(y)$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nSo, we have that $f(y)$ is positive for $y\\in (2,\\infty ),$ and negative for $y\\in (-\\infty ,2).$\n\nWe can now draw the phase line for this equation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071359/assets/ac2d3df6e9caa672e16f3499502bba9e17c5d79dd200055319c22bc29fb78340.png)\n\nFinally, we classify the equilibrium solution:\n\n- $y=-2$ is a source because the nearby solutions diverge away from this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$y=-2$ is a source\"." 13194139535952 true] [17592186376143 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376144 13194139535952 true] [17592186376143 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376145 13194139535952 true] [17592186376143 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376146 13194139535952 true] [17592186376143 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376147 13194139535952 true] [17592186376143 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376148 13194139535952 true] [17592186376143 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535952 true] [17592186376143 1041 "selection" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376143 1104 #edb/ref 17592186376144 13194139535952 true] [17592186376143 1110 #uuid "8cb6e6b4-dbda-5053-981d-78e441cb259b" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376144 1034 "$y=-2$ is a source" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376144 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535952 true] [17592186376144 1111 #uuid "5efec162-dfd7-5d56-8603-5427baed3bcf" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376145 1034 "$y=-2$ is a sink and $y=2$ is a source" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376145 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535952 true] [17592186376145 1111 #uuid "a3461d9d-84d3-53b6-b0d4-708719f99a06" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376146 1034 "$y=-2$ is a node" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376146 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535952 true] [17592186376146 1111 #uuid "d06eae3a-ee13-5a52-9291-9ad56da88bbf" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376147 1034 "$y=-2$ is a source and $y=2$ is a sink" 13194139535952 true] [17592186376147 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535952 true] [17592186376147 1111 #uuid "b63fcaaf-89e8